-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-03

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 4 recordings, 33534 frames, default colours, on the
              whole alt ROM build (2026-11-04: alt ROM image 1 is Sinclair's
              48K ROM plus the hooks, 0x0000-0x3FFF all written by the build):
              original and patched machines in lockstep, the patched machine's
              ROM 1 modelled as the Next fills it, NextZXOS's ROM3 first then
              the build's writes, so the IM 2 handler's jumps to 0x0038 run
              that image; hook instructions uncounted, whole 128K compared
              each frame apart from the screen pixels and the draw buffers
              built from them; sprite layer and ULA against an independent
              model at 3625 stable frames, including the Bridge's seated crew
              as sprite tiles (5 Bridge builds, 512 crew checks); 25,064 hook
              exits with registers checked; 19 of 19 negatives detected, the 3
              crew negatives on a recording that reaches the Bridge, and the
              new one, the previous build's image (hooks only over ROM3),
              detected by the lockstep from frame 1; unit tests pass including
              a full sprite pool and pictures inside windows; the UPDATE
              attribute option is neutralised and has no lockstep replay, only
              a check that its flag stays 0

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, whole alt ROM build (2026-11-04): menu,
              story screens, play, the command window and the Transporter Room
              reached, frames viewed; the alt ROM image dumped in JNext equals
              the modelled Sinclair-plus-hooks image; with NextZXOS's DivMMC
              0x0038 trap removed, IM 1 ran Sinclair's handler 3,977 times and
              the game played on, where the previous build reset to the
              Browser; earlier, on the previous build: the Knight walking past
              the Bridge's crew, command window, game over and return to the
              title, real loader from the Browser, MD5 exact

  Coverage    all 48 rooms entered by poked room change, with all objects and
              all 6 character graphics placed by cheat; walking, jumping,
              menus and commands; game over, new game; story puzzles,
              transporter trips by play and the ending not reached; cheats
              from the archive's 128K POKEs, time and others' stats held in
              the simulator on the original code, strength and fuel not run,
              all unplayed by a person; whole alt ROM image from 2026-11-04:
              the previous build differs only in the alt ROM fill (stub) and
              the alt ROM image's page bytes

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
